From f4d8aee8f7e71f7a0d216d57cd2ede70a6536e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <fwupd@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:48:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] genesys: Support level 1 MStar scalers with no public
 key

The MStar scalers supported so far report level 0 and hold an RSA public
key, which identifies the product and is matched against the key
appended to the firmware. Level 1 scalers such as the MST9U have no key
at all: the read returns unrelated data, so probe() rejected them as
having an invalid public-key and the panel never appeared.

Accept a level 1 scaler without a key and treat its firmware as a raw
image rather than a payload with a key appended. Scalers that do not
report level 1 keep the existing hard failure, so a real key read
failure is still an error.

Such a scaler reports a firmware ID rather than a version, made up of a
panel type and two release digits, e.g. EIM121 then EIM162. Only the
panel type survives an update, so that is what the GUID uses, scoped
with the hub's vendor and product IDs to limit the match to one product.

The update is written to image B, so reject a firmware file that places
image B at a different offset. Reading the firmware back returns image B
without parsing it, as the slot is larger than the file and the level 1
parser requires the updater trailer at the end. Level 0 scalers keep the
previous read-back behaviour.

Document the level 1 image layout and instance IDs in the README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
